Subject: [PATCH] Keep hwsim backhaul beacons while closing unrooted admission

Separate beacon availability from the generation-bound root admission gate.
On hwsim, disconnect and flush downstream stations without stopping the AP;
reject station creation and authorization while the parent is unproved.
Keep fronthauls untouched and retain the old shutdown path if the kernel
station flush fails. Non-hwsim targets retain AP shutdown until their
admission behavior is qualified. Readmission leaves a running AP untouched;
recovery of a stopped AP resets hostapd before setup, avoiding a restart of
an already-started BSS. Flush children even when cached bss_started is false;
a verified down netdevice needs no kernel flush and cannot block STA startup.

Upstream-Status: Pending

